n of parallelity in the midsagittal plane</article-title><source>Acta Psychol</source><year>2002</year><volume>109</volume><fpage>25</fpage><lpage>40</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0001-6918(01)00047-6</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Kappers AML (2002) Haptic perception of parallelity in the midsagittal plane. Acta Psychol 109:25&#x02013;40 </citation></ref><ref id="CR17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kappers</surname><given-names>AML</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Large systematic deviations in a bimanual parallelity task: further analysis of contributing factors</article-title><source>Acta Psychol</source><year>2003</year><volume>114</volume><fpage>131</fpage><lpage>145</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0001-6918(03)00063-5</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Kappers AML (2003) Large systematic deviations in a bimanual parallelity task: further analysis of contributing factors. Acta Psychol 114:131&#x02013;145 </citation></ref><ref id="CR18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kappers</surname><given-names>AML</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The contributions of egocentric and allocentric reference frames in haptic spatial tasks</article-title><source>Acta Psychol</source><year>2004</year><volume>117</volume><fpage>333</fpage><lpage>340</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.actpsy.2004.08.002</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Kappers AML (2004) The contributions of egocentric and allocentric reference frames in haptic spatial tasks. Acta Psychol 117:333&#x02013;340 </citation></ref><ref id="CR19"><citation citation-type="other">Kappers AML (2005) Intermediate frames of reference in haptically perceived parallelity. In: World haptics conference (WHC 2005): First joint eurohaptics conference and symp